-- GROUP G6: drug.unsuitable_population states each group to avoid the drug as the label words it ('nursing mothers', 'geriatric patients', 'renal insufficiency', 'patients with glaucoma'); G6a needs standard population groups, G6b the stated conditions
-- TYPE: fine-vs-coarse
-- COLUMN: drug.unsuitable_population
-- NOTE: FORM G6a rewrites each label's list to the standard groups it names: pregnancy (pregnant, pregnancy, planning to become pregnant); breastfeeding (breast-feeding, breast feeding, nursing mothers/women/infants); children (children, pediatric patients, adolescents, infants, newborns, children under N); elderly (older adults, geriatric patients, old age); kidney problems (kidney, renal, nephropathy, creatinine clearance, eGFR); liver problems (liver, hepatic, transaminases, AST/ALT, bilirubin); anything else becomes 'other conditions'.
-- NOTE: Children rule: an item that restricts only children with a condition ('children taking ibuprofen or ASA', 'children allergic to ...', 'children right before or after heart surgery', 'pediatric patients with pneumonia who ...') is a condition, not a warning against use in children. Animal rule (two veterinary labels): pregnant and nursing animals count as pregnancy and breastfeeding; young puppies, pets and dogs with conditions are other conditions.
